1
00:00:28,987 --> 00:00:30,613
These damn useless bastards.

2
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:34,451
This is fucking exhausting.
What was all that money for?

3
00:00:35,827 --> 00:00:38,121
Do I even fucking have a signal here?

4
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:53,595
This mountain feels fucking off.

5
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:19,454
Han-su, we need that bastard fast.
He got me good.

6
00:01:19,537 --> 00:01:21,581
That bastard's the fake one! Fuck!

7
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:28,671
When did he disappear?

8
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:30,799
I saw him falling behind
and panting earlier.

9
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:33,176
Why? What now?

10
00:01:33,927 --> 00:01:37,305
Apparently, he's the fake one.
We need to find him fast.

11
00:01:37,388 --> 00:01:39,641
I thought he was the real one!

12
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:25,228
MOUSETRAP

13
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:28,690
What? The fucking cops
smuggled the suspect out?

14
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:31,317
Those fuckers played me?

15
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:33,278
If I catch them, they're fucking dead.

16
00:02:33,361 --> 00:02:35,405
Hey, ask HQ for support.

17
00:02:35,488 --> 00:02:36,489
Now!

18
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:30,668
<i>You won't find your uncle.</i>
<i>This is your last chance.</i>

19
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:32,754
<i>Let's meet. It's time to end this.</i>

20
00:03:32,837 --> 00:03:33,796
Yes, sir.

21
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:35,798
I can't hear you. Say that again.

22
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:42,597
We're following the trail.

23
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:43,681
What? Who?

24
00:03:44,641 --> 00:03:47,435
Yeah, he came with us.
He said he wanted to help.

25
00:04:07,747 --> 00:04:09,123
Hey, this is it.

26
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:13,795
Where is that bastard?

27
00:04:13,878 --> 00:04:16,547
About 200 meters up
from the transmission tower.

28
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:20,551
This is fucking bullshit.

29
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:21,803
Fucking hell.

30
00:04:22,512 --> 00:04:24,931
Let's come back in daylight.
We can't see a thing.

31
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:28,851
Hey.

32
00:04:29,852 --> 00:04:31,896
If we lose the old man
and this goes south,

33
00:04:32,397 --> 00:04:33,398
I'll lose the money.

34
00:04:33,481 --> 00:04:35,024
You gonna cover it?

35
00:04:36,401 --> 00:04:39,362
Going through all this bullshit
just to take a loss?

36
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:42,282
We might as well fucking die.

37
00:04:42,365 --> 00:04:44,742
What's the point of even living?
Don't you think?

38
00:04:45,451 --> 00:04:47,495
Fuck. Seriously.

39
00:04:52,875 --> 00:04:53,918
Damn it.

40
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:01,718
My knees. For fuck's sake.

41
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:14,564
Who is it?

42
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:17,775
Is it that bastard?

43
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:20,737
No, just some guy I know.

44
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:25,366
Just ask that dumbass where he is.

45
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:28,453
Where the fuck is 200 meters
up from the tower?!

46
00:05:28,536 --> 00:05:30,705
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

47
00:05:38,963 --> 00:05:40,214
Guys, let's hurry up a bit.

48
00:05:40,298 --> 00:05:41,758
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

49
00:07:41,043 --> 00:07:43,129
AT THE TOWER NOW
WHERE'S 200 M UP FROM HERE?

50
00:07:51,345 --> 00:07:52,722
Are you almost here?

51
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:57,143
We've got a problem here.
Come help me out now.

52
00:08:18,748 --> 00:08:19,707
<i>Hey, be careful!</i>

53
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,211
- Who do we find first?
- Is that even a question?

54
00:08:23,794 --> 00:08:25,254
The perp, obviously.

55
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:27,006
If we let the suspect slip away,

56
00:08:27,089 --> 00:08:28,341
we'll end up in prison.

57
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:31,177
Someone's life is at stake here.

58
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:32,929
Shouldn't we save him first?

59
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:35,056
Damn it. We don't even know if he's alive.

60
00:08:35,139 --> 00:08:37,475
- Save him? Nah.
- Then the suspect first?

61
00:08:37,558 --> 00:08:39,060
No!

62
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:41,270
Let's just go down for now, okay?

63
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:45,691
We can't see a damn thing.
How are we supposed to find anything?

64
00:08:46,442 --> 00:08:47,693
- Sir.
- Yeah?

65
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:50,571
Let's head down
and come back in the morning

66
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:51,697
once the sun's up!

67
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:54,492
- Dong-cheol!
- Are you okay?

68
00:08:54,575 --> 00:08:55,826
Are you okay?

69
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:56,744
Hey, Dong-cheol…

70
00:08:56,827 --> 00:08:57,745
- What's this?
- Huh?

71
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:00,873
Hey.

72
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:02,542
This was dug recently.

73
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:04,544
Someone tried to bury something.

74
00:09:06,170 --> 00:09:08,130
The old man's alive. Let's find him first.

75
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:09,215
- Okay?
- Yes, sir.

76
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:10,758
Grab my hand.

77
00:09:13,636 --> 00:09:14,720
Okay.

78
00:09:15,888 --> 00:09:17,348
What? An abandoned building?

79
00:09:17,848 --> 00:09:20,059
Sir, apparently,
there's something up there.

80
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:26,566
Huh?

81
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:29,485
Huh?

82
00:09:31,571 --> 00:09:33,364
That's Noja's…

83
00:09:33,990 --> 00:09:36,117
Hey, catch him. Get him!

84
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:39,537
Come here!

85
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:40,705
Hey, come here!

86
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:42,373
Hey, stop right there!

87
00:09:42,456 --> 00:09:44,834
Hey, stop! I said stop!

88
00:09:45,334 --> 00:09:46,794
- Hey!
- Hey!

89
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:48,671
Hey, just stop already!

90
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:50,590
I said stop!

91
00:10:07,356 --> 00:10:08,733
Hey!

92
00:10:08,816 --> 00:10:10,192
Stop, damn it! Huh?

93
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:11,611
Hey, stop right there!

94
00:10:11,694 --> 00:10:12,695
Hey, stop!

95
00:10:12,778 --> 00:10:14,614
Hey, I said stop right there!

96
00:10:16,657 --> 00:10:18,075
Stop!

97
00:10:20,661 --> 00:10:21,912
- Hey, I said stop!
- Stop!

98
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:23,914
Hey!

99
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:41,140
What the fuck?

100
00:10:43,017 --> 00:10:44,268
Everyone, be careful.

101
00:10:45,269 --> 00:10:46,771
I think there's something here.

102
00:10:48,356 --> 00:10:49,523
Let's go.

103
00:10:54,487 --> 00:10:55,488
Damn it.

104
00:10:55,571 --> 00:10:57,323
Goddamn it.

105
00:10:59,909 --> 00:11:00,785
Hey, Min-ho.

106
00:11:01,535 --> 00:11:02,870
Chang-u, Dong-cheol.

107
00:11:15,466 --> 00:11:16,300
Second floor!

108
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:17,468
- Second floor!
- Where?

109
00:11:17,551 --> 00:11:18,761
- Second floor!
- Second?

110
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:20,096
- Second floor!
- Where?

111
00:11:34,402 --> 00:11:35,569
Find anything?

112
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:36,654
Nothing.

113
00:11:38,155 --> 00:11:39,573
Dong-cheol, Chang-u.

114
00:11:39,657 --> 00:11:40,491
Anything?

115
00:11:40,574 --> 00:11:43,911
What do you even expect to be here?
Maybe ghosts.

116
00:11:43,994 --> 00:11:45,830
You sure you checked properly, punk?

117
00:11:47,623 --> 00:11:49,333
There's not a damn thing.

118
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:51,961
- Damn it.
- What the hell?

119
00:11:54,004 --> 00:11:55,423
It's Sun-yong.

120
00:11:56,465 --> 00:11:57,299
Hello?

121
00:11:57,967 --> 00:12:01,262
Yeah, the pit.

122
00:12:01,345 --> 00:12:02,388
Yeah.

123
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:05,349
You haven't found him yet?

124
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:07,268
Where are you right now?

125
00:12:09,228 --> 00:12:10,604
An abandoned building?

126
00:12:11,313 --> 00:12:13,065
Out here in the woods?

127
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:16,861
Hey.

128
00:12:17,403 --> 00:12:18,404
Hang up.

129
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:35,838
- What the hell?
- Did you see a guy running by here?

130
00:12:35,921 --> 00:12:36,922
You're not dead?

131
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:40,760
- I'm still young. As if I'd die.
- Fucking hell.

132
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:42,303
You just won't die.

133
00:12:42,386 --> 00:12:44,722
If I'm late, Je Moon-jae will die!

134
00:12:44,805 --> 00:12:45,681
Hey.

135
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:49,059
That Je Moon-jae you were always with.

136
00:12:49,143 --> 00:12:50,478
He's the fake one.

137
00:12:51,312 --> 00:12:53,981
That bastard was with us and ran off.

138
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:57,359
That son of a bitch had us both fooled!

139
00:12:57,443 --> 00:12:58,486
Fuck.

140
00:12:58,569 --> 00:12:59,445
What?

141
00:13:00,488 --> 00:13:02,823
Guess I'll have to kill that bastard too.

142
00:13:03,824 --> 00:13:06,827
Let's not complicate things.
We just need to find the uncle.

143
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:08,496
He's somewhere on this mountain.

144
00:13:08,579 --> 00:13:09,914
DNA.

145
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:12,666
Once we do the DNA test, it's all over.

146
00:13:14,585 --> 00:13:18,255
Hey, you do it your way.
I'll do it my way.

147
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:21,217
That damn…

148
00:13:29,016 --> 00:13:32,311
What the fuck are those bastards doing?

149
00:13:32,394 --> 00:13:34,522
What the fuck is even on this mountain?

150
00:13:34,605 --> 00:13:38,067
That bastard wasn't telling us everything.

151
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:39,527
Sir, those bastards…

152
00:13:40,986 --> 00:13:43,405
They must be working with the suspect.

153
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:47,076
Still, the entire Criminal Investigations
Division is in on this shit?

154
00:13:48,035 --> 00:13:49,328
Hey. Get your gear.

155
00:13:49,411 --> 00:13:50,996
- Yes, sir.
- Let them handle it here.

156
00:13:51,622 --> 00:13:53,707
We'll go up first. Stay focused.

157
00:13:53,791 --> 00:13:55,751
If we mess this up,
all our heads will roll.

158
00:13:55,835 --> 00:13:57,711
- Got it?
- Got it.

159
00:14:13,018 --> 00:14:16,272
If you get caught now, you're dead,
you fucking dumbass.

160
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,906
<i>How about you two?</i>

161
00:14:26,699 --> 00:14:28,450
Do you trust that guy?

162
00:14:32,037 --> 00:14:33,914
Isn't it about time

163
00:14:33,998 --> 00:14:36,542
you guys went out on your own?

164
00:14:36,625 --> 00:14:38,961
You wanna fucking die?
Watch your fucking mouth.

165
00:14:39,044 --> 00:14:40,462
Hey, fucker,

166
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:42,673
you think we're suckers like Myeong-su?

167
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:44,174
You fucking bastard, I'll…

168
00:14:45,092 --> 00:14:47,052
That's not what I meant.

169
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:50,055
Myeong-su went
straight to the police station.

170
00:14:50,556 --> 00:14:55,019
And once this is over,
he'll use you two to kill me.

171
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:58,022
Should I get insurance?

172
00:14:58,105 --> 00:15:00,065
That just crossed my mind.

173
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:09,366
I mean, knowing him,

174
00:15:09,867 --> 00:15:12,077
I don't think
he'll give you any severance.

175
00:15:13,245 --> 00:15:14,079
Right?

176
00:15:15,539 --> 00:15:16,373
Oh,

177
00:15:16,999 --> 00:15:19,501
I'm not saying you guys should betray him.

178
00:15:19,585 --> 00:15:22,046
Just in case things go south…

179
00:15:22,129 --> 00:15:23,380
Insurance, you know.

180
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:26,592
Insurance that only pays out
after an incident.

181
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:36,977
I don't care who gets the money.
I just need to stay alive.

182
00:15:38,103 --> 00:15:39,647
Just pretend you didn't hear it.

183
00:15:40,898 --> 00:15:42,358
That bastard texted me.

184
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:44,693
He wants you alive.

185
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:47,655
He said you two had
some fucking unfinished business.

186
00:16:00,167 --> 00:16:01,961
Where is he? Where did he go?

187
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:06,340
Weren't we here to find that old man?

188
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,592
Why are we chasing this guy?

189
00:16:09,093 --> 00:16:13,097
You fucking dumbass.
Why do you think he suddenly showed up?

190
00:16:14,306 --> 00:16:17,768
Didn't you think he'd be trouble
if he found the old man first?

191
00:16:19,937 --> 00:16:20,771
Hey.

192
00:16:23,273 --> 00:16:24,191
Hold on.

193
00:16:32,866 --> 00:16:34,618
Is something up with you two?

194
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:36,620
What do you…

195
00:16:38,330 --> 00:16:42,167
Then why the fuck
can't you just do as you're told?

196
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:46,422
Who texted you earlier?

197
00:16:47,798 --> 00:16:49,091
Just some guy you know?

198
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:51,427
There's some guy you know that I don't?

199
00:16:56,932 --> 00:16:58,559
Where's your brother?

200
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,479
He went on ahead to find him.

201
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:07,776
You fucking bastard.
Then what are you doing? Go after him.

202
00:17:08,944 --> 00:17:09,778
I will.

203
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:13,115
Fuck.

204
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:16,827
For fuck's sake. Damn it.

205
00:17:17,327 --> 00:17:18,412
Fuck this.

206
00:17:39,558 --> 00:17:40,851
You fucking bastard!

207
00:17:54,364 --> 00:17:55,741
Fuck!

208
00:18:05,042 --> 00:18:05,959
Hey.

209
00:18:07,252 --> 00:18:08,378
Did you prove

210
00:18:09,213 --> 00:18:10,339
who you are?

211
00:18:28,565 --> 00:18:30,275
<i>When I was in university,</i>

212
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:32,778
there was this guy named Seo Yu-min.

213
00:18:34,404 --> 00:18:36,240
I've never heard that name before.

214
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:42,955
There was this guy.

215
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:46,708
He had everything I didn't.

216
00:18:48,001 --> 00:18:49,920
Every time I saw him, I'd think,

217
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:53,632
"I wish I were him."

218
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:07,437
Hey, did you write this?

219
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:10,482
Yeah. How is it? You think it's good?

220
00:19:11,608 --> 00:19:12,651
It's insane.

221
00:19:13,152 --> 00:19:15,320
You can't just leave it here to rot.

222
00:19:16,113 --> 00:19:18,198
But I'm too lazy.

223
00:19:18,282 --> 00:19:20,450
I still have this much to write,
but I'm stuck.

224
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:47,394
<i>It was a truly amazing story.</i>

225
00:19:48,228 --> 00:19:51,106
It was so amazing,
I couldn't get it out of my head for days.

226
00:19:52,774 --> 00:19:55,402
But Yu-min was so lazy,
he never bothered writing it.

227
00:19:56,528 --> 00:19:57,571
<i>A few days later,</i>

228
00:19:57,654 --> 00:19:59,823
<i>the club opened submissions</i>
<i>for its anthology.</i>

229
00:20:01,950 --> 00:20:04,578
I think I started writing like crazy
that night.

230
00:20:04,661 --> 00:20:06,997
<i>Trying to remember</i>
<i>as much of it as I could.</i>

231
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:44,284
<i>Even if I stole it,</i>

232
00:20:44,868 --> 00:20:46,536
<i>it'd be fine if nobody found out.</i>

233
00:20:52,751 --> 00:20:54,086
Just read these. You'll see.

234
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:57,881
That every novel I've written so far,

235
00:20:58,465 --> 00:20:59,591
I stole from there.

236
00:21:08,976 --> 00:21:11,687
Why are you telling me this?

237
00:21:12,896 --> 00:21:13,772
Huh?

238
00:21:17,359 --> 00:21:19,319
You already know I'm not Je Moon-jae.

239
00:21:23,490 --> 00:21:24,825
Who do you think I am?

240
00:21:37,212 --> 00:21:38,046
This person.

241
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:40,674
Every novel Je Moon-jae wrote

242
00:21:40,757 --> 00:21:41,758
is mine.

243
00:21:43,218 --> 00:21:44,886
He was a fake from the start.

244
00:21:56,815 --> 00:21:58,859
Publish it as planned.

245
00:21:59,359 --> 00:22:00,902
It'll be a big hit.

246
00:22:00,986 --> 00:22:01,820
THE RAT

247
00:22:01,903 --> 00:22:03,113
It hasn't been edited.

248
00:22:03,196 --> 00:22:04,740
I didn't have time.

249
00:22:06,742 --> 00:22:08,076
It'll be the same anyway.

250
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:10,746
The ending, at least.

251
00:22:32,684 --> 00:22:33,727
Damn it.

252
00:22:38,482 --> 00:22:39,316
Damn it.

253
00:22:53,622 --> 00:22:54,748
Damn it.

254
00:23:12,974 --> 00:23:13,809
What the…

255
00:23:23,276 --> 00:23:24,528
Did you find him?

256
00:23:24,611 --> 00:23:25,570
- Hey, Sun-yong!
- Sir!

257
00:23:25,654 --> 00:23:26,863
Oh man.

258
00:23:26,947 --> 00:23:30,075
Hey, why is it raining
on such a clear, moonlit night?

259
00:23:30,158 --> 00:23:32,327
- See anyone else on your way here?
- Just a pit.

260
00:23:32,411 --> 00:23:33,870
I saw the pit too.

261
00:23:33,954 --> 00:23:35,789
Let's find the old man, our only lead.

262
00:23:35,872 --> 00:23:37,457
There's a trail leading this way.

263
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:39,209
- But no one's here.
- So…

264
00:23:39,292 --> 00:23:41,878
You said that guy was a fake.
What was that about?

265
00:23:41,962 --> 00:23:44,673
Hey, if he's the fake one,
all our heads will roll.

266
00:23:44,756 --> 00:23:46,675
Not our heads. We'll be behind bars!

267
00:23:46,758 --> 00:23:47,968
- Enough.
- Come on.

268
00:23:48,593 --> 00:23:50,178
Fuck it. I'll take the fall.

269
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:51,805
I'm the boss here, you punk!

270
00:23:53,181 --> 00:23:55,058
What the hell is Min-ho doing up there?

271
00:23:55,142 --> 00:23:55,976
What?

272
00:23:58,562 --> 00:24:00,355
- Hey, Min-ho!
- You're here.

273
00:24:00,439 --> 00:24:01,273
Anything?

274
00:24:01,356 --> 00:24:02,691
There's nothing.

275
00:24:14,411 --> 00:24:16,997
Noja, what happened? You're alive?

276
00:24:18,832 --> 00:24:19,749
What are you doing?

277
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:21,668
Who are you, you fucking bastard?

278
00:24:21,751 --> 00:24:22,586
Wait. Let's talk.

279
00:24:27,174 --> 00:24:28,300
You've got five seconds.

280
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:37,017
Five seconds are up.

281
00:24:37,517 --> 00:24:38,393
Go on.

282
00:24:39,686 --> 00:24:40,604
Kill me.

283
00:24:47,861 --> 00:24:49,404
The Rat sent this.

284
00:24:49,905 --> 00:24:52,282
You said someone else needed to prove it.

285
00:25:04,252 --> 00:25:07,005
YOU WON'T FIND YOUR UNCLE
THIS IS YOUR LAST CHANCE

286
00:25:07,088 --> 00:25:08,131
Funny, isn't it?

287
00:25:08,632 --> 00:25:11,384
That the guy impersonating me is my proof.

288
00:25:12,761 --> 00:25:13,595
I'll go meet him.

289
00:25:14,679 --> 00:25:16,139
It's time to end this.

290
00:25:20,143 --> 00:25:20,977
Then let's go.

291
00:25:22,270 --> 00:25:23,104
Let's see

292
00:25:24,397 --> 00:25:26,191
who ends up like that at the end.

293
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:29,986
Let's fucking go.

294
00:25:51,591 --> 00:25:52,425
Hey!

295
00:25:55,512 --> 00:25:56,763
Where are you going?

296
00:25:57,389 --> 00:25:58,223
Sorry?

297
00:26:01,142 --> 00:26:03,019
Why do I keep getting this feeling?

298
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:06,398
Like I'm walking toward my own grave.

299
00:26:07,691 --> 00:26:09,943
- What do you--
- Fucking hell.

300
00:26:10,443 --> 00:26:12,654
I don't hear anything around here.

301
00:26:12,737 --> 00:26:13,905
Where are you going?

302
00:26:14,906 --> 00:26:16,324
I heard a noise over there, so…

303
00:26:19,911 --> 00:26:21,746
Seriously, where's your brother?

304
00:26:21,830 --> 00:26:23,748
No idea. He's not answering his phone.

305
00:26:30,797 --> 00:26:32,215
Fucking hell.

306
00:26:40,181 --> 00:26:41,099
Give me your phone.

307
00:26:41,182 --> 00:26:42,767
Why do you need my phone?

308
00:26:42,851 --> 00:26:44,102
Just give it to me.

309
00:26:44,185 --> 00:26:46,646
Something from a few days ago
won't leave my mind.

310
00:26:48,315 --> 00:26:49,149
Huh?

311
00:26:49,941 --> 00:26:50,775
What is it?

312
00:26:53,069 --> 00:26:55,530
Looks like you have a reason
not to show me your phone.

313
00:26:56,448 --> 00:26:58,158
Seems like there's something

314
00:26:58,783 --> 00:26:59,784
I shouldn't

315
00:27:00,493 --> 00:27:01,328
know about.

316
00:27:07,042 --> 00:27:08,543
What did that rat bastard say?

317
00:27:11,755 --> 00:27:12,672
Not to…

318
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:15,508
Not to kill the guy
who's always with Noja.

319
00:27:22,349 --> 00:27:25,477
But why did he text that to you guys
instead of me?

320
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:28,980
He said you'll kill him anyway.

321
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:31,816
That we won't get paid when it's all over.

322
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:34,444
So he suggested we go our own way.

323
00:27:36,279 --> 00:27:38,406
You bastard.

324
00:27:39,407 --> 00:27:42,661
After you saw what happened to Myeong-su,
you fucking idiots…

325
00:27:45,413 --> 00:27:46,289
I'm sorry.

326
00:27:46,373 --> 00:27:47,749
Please spare me.

327
00:27:54,255 --> 00:27:56,007
Go out on your own, you bastard.

328
00:28:03,598 --> 00:28:06,351
Because of one fucking rat bastard…

329
00:28:06,434 --> 00:28:07,644
Everything's gone to shit.

330
00:28:13,191 --> 00:28:14,567
Hey, look inside there.

331
00:28:17,153 --> 00:28:18,822
What did you say was here?

332
00:28:18,905 --> 00:28:20,198
There's nothing?

333
00:28:21,032 --> 00:28:22,242
Nothing, you damn bastard.

334
00:28:22,325 --> 00:28:25,203
I told you.
We already searched here earlier!

335
00:28:25,286 --> 00:28:27,497
Where exactly did you see the shadow?

336
00:28:28,081 --> 00:28:28,998
Around here.

337
00:28:29,082 --> 00:28:30,291
Seriously! Goddamn it!

338
00:28:30,375 --> 00:28:32,043
- Chang-u, here.
- Yes, sir.

339
00:28:32,127 --> 00:28:33,336
Damn it.

340
00:28:35,171 --> 00:28:37,465
God, is this some kind of horror show?

341
00:28:39,342 --> 00:28:41,010
I saw it from outside. Fuck.

342
00:28:41,094 --> 00:28:42,679
I've checked this room a few times.

343
00:28:58,278 --> 00:28:59,279
Hasn't been that long.

344
00:28:59,362 --> 00:29:01,823
I guess they needed to dig a hole.

345
00:29:07,620 --> 00:29:10,081
Hey, it's that way. Let's go.

346
00:29:10,165 --> 00:29:11,040
Let's go.

347
00:29:12,125 --> 00:29:14,294
Hey, you look this way.

348
00:29:14,377 --> 00:29:16,337
You look that way. Okay?

349
00:29:28,099 --> 00:29:28,933
You bastard!

350
00:29:29,017 --> 00:29:30,185
- Get him!
- Hey!

351
00:29:30,268 --> 00:29:32,395
Hey, run!

352
00:29:32,479 --> 00:29:33,813
- You bastard! Stop!
- Stop!

353
00:29:33,897 --> 00:29:35,732
- Hey!
- You bastard.

354
00:29:36,524 --> 00:29:37,525
Stop right there!

355
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:15,688
First floor!

356
00:30:15,772 --> 00:30:16,731
First floor!

357
00:30:17,232 --> 00:30:18,066
First floor!

358
00:30:18,149 --> 00:30:18,983
First floor?

359
00:30:19,067 --> 00:30:20,193
- Huh?
- First floor!

360
00:30:20,276 --> 00:30:22,320
First floor? Where on the first floor?

361
00:30:30,787 --> 00:30:32,330
Hurry! Get down there!

362
00:30:33,122 --> 00:30:34,082
I'll go this way!

363
00:30:34,165 --> 00:30:35,625
- Where?
- First floor!

364
00:30:45,885 --> 00:30:48,096
Hey! There he is! Go!

365
00:30:48,179 --> 00:30:49,889
You bastard! Stop right there!

366
00:30:49,973 --> 00:30:51,349
Huh?

367
00:30:51,432 --> 00:30:53,184
What? Sir! What the hell?

368
00:30:53,268 --> 00:30:54,227
- Up ahead!
- Get him!

369
00:30:54,310 --> 00:30:55,311
Hey! Over there!

370
00:30:59,858 --> 00:31:01,943
- What's there?
- Just hurry up and go!

371
00:31:02,026 --> 00:31:03,903
- He went down!
- What is it?

372
00:31:17,375 --> 00:31:18,710
- Fuck.
- Min-ho, Chang-u.

373
00:31:18,793 --> 00:31:20,503
Catch the guy who ran away.

374
00:31:21,671 --> 00:31:23,047
Go. Now.

375
00:31:31,639 --> 00:31:32,473
<i>Next up is</i>

376
00:31:33,099 --> 00:31:34,642
that bastard you were always with.

377
00:31:35,226 --> 00:31:36,185
Don't you get it?

378
00:31:36,686 --> 00:31:38,813
That bastard isn't working with you!

379
00:31:38,897 --> 00:31:40,815
He's using you!

380
00:31:41,316 --> 00:31:43,568
You'll end up like me!

381
00:31:52,493 --> 00:31:55,163
You used me? You're fucking dead.

382
00:32:18,853 --> 00:32:19,979
What the hell?

383
00:32:24,734 --> 00:32:27,153
I'll blow your heads off.
You fucking bastards!

384
00:32:28,696 --> 00:32:30,615
Fucking sons of bitches!

385
00:32:31,115 --> 00:32:34,077
Why are you running with the bastards
who killed cops? Huh?

386
00:32:34,953 --> 00:32:36,663
Hey! Cuff these bastards!

387
00:32:38,957 --> 00:32:39,999
It broke on its own!

388
00:32:40,083 --> 00:32:40,917
No!

389
00:32:42,251 --> 00:32:43,503
It just snapped.

390
00:32:44,087 --> 00:32:45,338
Come on, this is…

391
00:32:45,421 --> 00:32:46,422
Hey, don't!

392
00:32:47,757 --> 00:32:48,758
Hey!

393
00:32:55,056 --> 00:32:59,602
Smuggling a suspect and working with him?
You call yourself a fucking cop?

394
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:01,354
Come on, put the gun away.

395
00:33:01,437 --> 00:33:04,107
There must be a misunderstanding.
He fooled us too.

396
00:33:04,190 --> 00:33:05,483
Get your hand off.

397
00:33:05,566 --> 00:33:06,734
You fucking bastard!

398
00:33:06,818 --> 00:33:09,237
Sun-yong, stop! No!

399
00:33:09,320 --> 00:33:10,238
Fuck!

400
00:33:12,073 --> 00:33:13,241
Hey, stop it!

401
00:33:16,869 --> 00:33:19,706
Did you hear me? I said stop!

402
00:33:43,771 --> 00:33:45,565
Hey, you fucking bastards!

403
00:33:45,648 --> 00:33:47,650
Stop!

404
00:33:52,280 --> 00:33:53,531
What the fuck?

405
00:33:57,076 --> 00:33:58,953
Dong-cheol, Chang-u, Min-ho!

406
00:33:59,037 --> 00:34:00,747
Who the hell are they?

407
00:34:01,330 --> 00:34:03,708
Who the hell are you punks?

408
00:34:04,667 --> 00:34:05,626
Get behind.

409
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:06,753
Hey! Stop them!

410
00:34:07,253 --> 00:34:09,255
Don't move! You bastards! Damn it.

411
00:34:09,338 --> 00:34:10,465
Stop them!

412
00:34:51,214 --> 00:34:52,840
Are you sleeping, you bastard?

413
00:34:52,924 --> 00:34:54,092
Get up quickly!

414
00:35:06,729 --> 00:35:08,147
You fucking bastard!

415
00:35:08,648 --> 00:35:09,524
Min-ho!

416
00:35:16,614 --> 00:35:17,490
Chang-u, get him!

417
00:35:17,990 --> 00:35:19,867
You bastard. Move!

418
00:35:19,951 --> 00:35:21,994
We're the Korean police! You bastard!

419
00:35:31,921 --> 00:35:33,172
- What?
- Fuck.

420
00:35:38,386 --> 00:35:39,762
Search every inch!

421
00:35:39,846 --> 00:35:41,389
- Got it!
- Yes, got it!

422
00:35:41,472 --> 00:35:42,640
Do you see anything?

423
00:35:44,433 --> 00:35:45,601
We're fucked.

424
00:35:46,310 --> 00:35:47,562
Totally fucked.

425
00:35:50,189 --> 00:35:51,482
A bit more this way!

426
00:35:53,067 --> 00:35:56,696
Noja, I'll draw them that way.
You go the other way.

427
00:35:59,073 --> 00:36:00,116
'Cause I'm faster.

428
00:36:01,742 --> 00:36:03,411
This is my problem anyway.

429
00:36:04,412 --> 00:36:07,498
Let's part ways here.
No need to get hurt because of me.

430
00:36:09,083 --> 00:36:10,543
This time, I'll help you.

431
00:36:14,755 --> 00:36:16,257
Hey, don't get hurt!

432
00:36:16,340 --> 00:36:17,675
Be careful when you go down!

433
00:36:18,259 --> 00:36:19,093
Here.

434
00:36:22,555 --> 00:36:23,848
Something for the road.

435
00:36:25,641 --> 00:36:27,143
This is all I have.

436
00:36:30,313 --> 00:36:32,899
I told you to close the gaps!

437
00:36:33,566 --> 00:36:34,400
Yes, got it!

438
00:36:34,901 --> 00:36:35,818
Moon-jae.

439
00:36:36,319 --> 00:36:37,653
Don't become a fake.

440
00:36:38,154 --> 00:36:39,780
No matter how shitty your life is,

441
00:36:40,281 --> 00:36:41,866
you've got to be the real one.

442
00:36:43,409 --> 00:36:45,203
Keep that in mind, you bastard!

443
00:36:52,418 --> 00:36:53,419
Noja.

444
00:36:54,128 --> 00:36:54,962
Noja!

445
00:36:55,046 --> 00:36:57,131
Hey, you bastards!

446
00:36:57,632 --> 00:36:58,758
Over here, you bastards!

447
00:36:59,675 --> 00:37:00,635
- Hey!
- He's there!

448
00:37:00,718 --> 00:37:02,261
- Hey! Get him!
- He's there!

449
00:37:02,345 --> 00:37:03,262
There!

450
00:37:03,346 --> 00:37:05,389
- Get him!
- Over there!

451
00:37:10,603 --> 00:37:12,438
- Don't lose him!
- Get him!

452
00:37:12,521 --> 00:37:14,523
- I said don't lose him!
- Get him!

453
00:37:18,861 --> 00:37:20,279
Get him! No matter what!

454
00:37:42,760 --> 00:37:44,136
Fuck!

455
00:37:44,220 --> 00:37:45,388
I said stop!

456
00:37:55,773 --> 00:37:56,816
Min-ho!

457
00:37:56,899 --> 00:37:58,484
Catch that old man!

458
00:38:08,286 --> 00:38:09,120
That bastard.

459
00:38:09,203 --> 00:38:11,247
Where's he going after causing this mess?

460
00:38:12,206 --> 00:38:13,416
Sir!

461
00:38:16,335 --> 00:38:17,461
Sir!

462
00:38:18,296 --> 00:38:19,380
Damn it.

463
00:38:19,922 --> 00:38:21,132
Sir!

464
00:38:21,882 --> 00:38:22,717
Where are you?

465
00:38:27,471 --> 00:38:28,723
Sir!

466
00:38:30,725 --> 00:38:32,310
Sir!

467
00:38:34,937 --> 00:38:35,938
<i>Moon-jae!</i>

468
00:38:39,108 --> 00:38:40,609
Moon-jae!

469
00:38:43,529 --> 00:38:45,489
Moon-jae, where are you?

470
00:38:46,866 --> 00:38:48,492
Moon-jae!

471
00:38:49,618 --> 00:38:50,870
Uncle!

472
00:38:50,953 --> 00:38:52,705
Where are you, Uncle?

473
00:38:57,752 --> 00:38:58,586
Uncle!

474
00:38:59,670 --> 00:39:01,047
Uncle!

475
00:39:17,855 --> 00:39:19,231
That fucking…

476
00:39:19,732 --> 00:39:21,150
Hey, you bastard!

477
00:39:56,185 --> 00:39:57,812
You son of a bitch.

478
00:40:08,781 --> 00:40:09,782
Sun-yong!

479
00:40:11,075 --> 00:40:12,368
Sun-yong!

480
00:40:13,119 --> 00:40:14,495
Sun-yong, are you okay?

481
00:40:14,578 --> 00:40:16,038
Huh? Are you okay?

482
00:40:16,122 --> 00:40:17,331
What?

483
00:40:19,917 --> 00:40:21,210
Why'd you go this far?

484
00:40:23,254 --> 00:40:24,964
You bastard! Get up, you punk!

485
00:40:25,923 --> 00:40:28,467
Sun-yong!

486
00:40:30,094 --> 00:40:32,763
<i>Living with this face was horrible.</i>

487
00:40:33,973 --> 00:40:36,600
<i>But it's over now, Je Moon-jae.</i>

488
00:41:15,848 --> 00:41:18,684
DATE OF INTERMENT: DECEMBER 5, 2022
NAME: UNKNOWN

489
00:41:28,027 --> 00:41:30,446
<i>I'm sorry I sent you off without a name.</i>

490
00:41:31,864 --> 00:41:36,035
<i>I wanted the world to know who killed you.</i>

491
00:41:37,411 --> 00:41:39,413
<i>That it was this face.</i>

492
00:41:40,706 --> 00:41:42,541
<i>At around 4:40 p.m. today,</i>

493
00:41:42,625 --> 00:41:45,920
<i>a passerby found a suspicious object</i>
<i>in the water</i>

494
00:41:46,003 --> 00:41:47,505
<i>and alerted authorities.</i>

495
00:41:47,588 --> 00:41:51,467
<i>The body was found floating in the water</i>
<i>and recovered by rescue teams.</i>

496
00:41:51,550 --> 00:41:54,428
<i>The deceased is believed to be a woman</i>
<i>in her early thirties,</i>

497
00:41:54,512 --> 00:41:57,014
<i>but her identity remains unknown.</i>

498
00:41:57,097 --> 00:41:58,557
<i>The body was immediately…</i>

499
00:42:03,687 --> 00:42:05,606
<i>It's been a long and painful time.</i>

500
00:42:07,608 --> 00:42:09,777
<i>You must've waited a long time too.</i>

501
00:42:12,905 --> 00:42:16,909
DATE OF INTERMENT: DECEMBER 5, 2022

502
00:42:16,992 --> 00:42:18,827
NAME: UNKNOWN

503
00:42:19,453 --> 00:42:20,704
<i>We're almost there.</i>

504
00:42:21,705 --> 00:42:22,998
<i>The end is near.</i>

505
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:26,126
<i>Je Moon-jae.</i>

506
00:42:26,835 --> 00:42:29,088
<i>You know where I'm headed.</i>

507
00:42:29,171 --> 00:42:31,507
<i>It's where all this began.</i>

508
00:42:31,590 --> 00:42:32,716
<i>That beach.</i>

509
00:42:33,217 --> 00:42:35,261
E-TICKET
DEPARTURE: SEOUL - ARRIVAL: JEJU

510
00:42:35,344 --> 00:42:36,762
<i>Let's end it</i>

511
00:42:37,805 --> 00:42:38,889
<i>where it started.</i>

512
00:47:19,461 --> 00:47:22,381
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
